cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SPECSIM3D: spectral simulation of anisotropic three-dimensional Gaussian random fields"
abstract: >-
  SPECSIM3D is a Fortran program (OpenMP) that generates unconditional and
  conditional realizations of stationary Gaussian random fields in three
  dimensions by the spectral random-phase method. It supports spherical,
  exponential and Gaussian covariance models, nested structures, a nugget
  effect and full geometric anisotropy, conditioning by kriging of the
  residual, and output in GSLIB, raw binary, VTK and VTK XML formats.
type: software
